Wayland protocols for pointer lock (../pointerlock.cpp) and activation tokens
(../activation.cpp), from wayland-protocols
(https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/wayland/wayland-protocols, unstable/ and
staging/), MIT licensed (see each XML). The C code is generated, so building
needs no wayland-scanner; after updating an XML, regenerate it:

  for p in pointer-constraints-unstable relative-pointer-unstable xdg-activation; do
    wayland-scanner client-header $p-v1.xml $p-v1-client-protocol.h
    wayland-scanner private-code $p-v1.xml $p-v1-protocol.c
  done
